<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Shah (Mughal emperor)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1702">1702</a>–<a href="/years/1748">1748</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Shah was Mughal emperor from 1719 to 1748. His long reign saw the provinces slip from central control as governors founded hereditary states in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Awadh</a>, where he appointed Saadat Ali Khan in 1722. In 1739 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> and carried off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peacock-throne">Peacock Throne</a>, a blow from which the empire never recovered.</p></div>
